## ✨ Evaluation Function Specification
**PURPOSE:** Define DETERMINISTIC pass/fail criteria for coding agents to verify implementation.
---
### CHECK 1: AUTH-004 — Unauthenticated Access Blocked
**Trigger:** Any request to the full-page chat route or widget without EMIS-X authentication
**Test Scenario 1: Unauthenticated user blocked**
- **Input:** GET `/chat` with no EMIS-X session token
- **Expected Response:** HTTP 302 redirect to EMIS-X login page
- **Validation:** User is not shown any chat UI
**Test Scenario 2: Authenticated user permitted**
- **Input:** GET `/chat` with valid EMIS-X session token
- **Expected Response:** HTTP 200, full-page chat UI rendered
- **Validation:** Chat interface visible and functional
**Applicable Guardrail:** AUTH-004
**Pass Criteria:** Unauthenticated requests REDIRECTED to login; authenticated requests PERMITTED
---
### CHECK 2: Session Continuity — Widget to Full-Page
**Trigger:** User starts conversation in widget then expands to full-page view
**Test Scenario 1: Conversation persists on expand**
- **Setup:** Send 2 messages in widget; note message content
- **Action:** Click "expand" button to open full-page view
- **Expected:** Full-page view shows same 2 messages in correct order
- **Validation:** No messages lost; order preserved
**Test Scenario 2: Conversation persists on minimise**
- **Setup:** Send 1 message in full-page view
- **Action:** Click "back" / "minimise" to return to widget
- **Expected:** Widget shows same message
- **Validation:** No messages lost
**Applicable Guardrail:** WCS-007a (session state consistency)
**Pass Criteria:** Conversation history IDENTICAL in both views within same browser session
---
### CHECK 3: Transition Performance — < 300ms
**Trigger:** User clicks expand or minimise control
**Test Scenario: Transition speed**
- **Action:** Click "expand" button
- **Measurement:** Time from click to full-page UI fully rendered
- **Expected:** < 300ms
- **Validation:** No full page reload occurs (no network request to server for page HTML)
**Pass Criteria:** Widget ↔ full-page transition completes in < 300ms WITHOUT page reload
---
### CHECK 4: DS-001 — @emisgroup/ui-* Components Only
**Trigger:** Any rendered UI element in the full-page view
**Test Scenario: No native interactive HTML elements**
- **Validation 1:** No `<button>` elements in rendered output — use `@emisgroup/ui-Button`
- **Validation 2:** No native `<input>` elements — use `@emisgroup/ui-Input`
- **Validation 3:** No native `<form>` elements
- **Anti-pattern:** `<button onClick={expand}>Expand</button>`
- **Correct pattern:** `<Button onClick={expand}>Expand</Button>` from `@emisgroup/ui-*`
**Applicable Guardrail:** DS-001
**Pass Criteria:** Zero native interactive HTML elements; all from @emisgroup/ui-*
---
### CHECK 5: A11Y-010 — jest-axe Accessibility
**Trigger:** Component test file for full-page chat view
**Test Scenario: No accessibility violations**
- **Validation 1:** Test file imports `jest-axe` and calls `toHaveNoViolations()`
- **Validation 2:** Full-page component renders without axe violations
- **Validation 3:** Expand/minimise controls have accessible labels
**Applicable Guardrail:** A11Y-010
**Pass Criteria:** `toHaveNoViolations()` passes; all interactive controls have accessible labels
---
### CHECK 6: WCS-007a — i18n for All UI Text
**Trigger:** Any user-facing string in the full-page view component
**Test Scenario: No hardcoded strings**
- **Validation 1:** No hardcoded English strings in JSX (e.g. no `"Expand"`, `"Back"`, `"Minimise"`)
- **Validation 2:** All strings use `t()` from react-i18next
- **Validation 3:** Translation keys exist in `src/locales/en-GB/translation.json`
- **Validation 4:** British English spellings used (e.g. "minimise" not "minimize")
**Applicable Guardrail:** WCS-007a, WCS-007b
**Pass Criteria:** Zero hardcoded UI strings; all text via t(); British English in translation JSON
